# Bytes here are load-bearing: every registry entry carries the canonical licence text's
# SHA-256, and the emitted artifacts are byte-compared between two runs of unchanged sources
# (VS-04, FS02-084). A CRLF checkout on Windows would change them, so the whole tree is
# pinned to LF. It was pinned first for the JCS/SHA-256 ledger chain and the CT entry hashes;
# those trees moved to the website on 2026-09-09 (FS-00 §6.10) and the reasons above stand
# on their own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Nothing here is binary today, but keep the door closed rather than ajar.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
